  concept: "Authored objective: Release and rearm.\nAuthored requirement: Recorded
    from solved raw and filtered voltages and observed counts. voltage \u2265 4.8
    V. voltage \u2264 5.2 V.\nGeneral teaching principle: Electrical measurements
    are differences or flows that require a correct reference, operating condition
    and fresh solver evidence.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish
    that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A pressure gauge needs a reference; a voltage measurement likewise depends
    on its defined points.
